# Vue Frontend Style

## Component structure
- `<template>` first, then `<script setup>` (plain JS, Composition API).
- Script section order: imports → composables (`useI18n`, `useRouter`, ...) → state (`reactive` form, `ref` flags) → action handlers → `onMounted` at the very bottom of the file.

## Translations
- Never hardcode user-facing text. Use `$t('section.key')` in templates and `t('...')` in script (via `useI18n`).
- Add every new key to both `web/src/locales/en.json` and `web/src/locales/fr.json`.

## API calls
- All HTTP calls go through the named exports of `@/api` (e.g. `setup_api`, `auth_api`). Never import axios or use `fetch` directly in components.
- If an endpoint is missing, add it to the matching `*_api` export in `web/src/api/index.js`.

## Self-contained actions
- A handler owns its whole flow. Inline single-use logic (validation, mapping) inside the handler instead of extracting top-level helpers used only once.

```js
// ❌ BAD: single-use helper at top level
const validateForm = () => { ... }
const handleSetup = async () => {
  if (!validateForm()) return
  ...
}

// ✅ GOOD: validation lives inside the handler
const handleSetup = async () => {
  if (form.adminPassword !== form.confirmPassword) {
    error.value = t('setup.error_passwords_match')
    return
  }
  ...
}
```

## State and errors
- Forms are one `reactive` object; UI flags (`loading`, `error`) are `ref`s.
- Async handlers: set `loading` true, clear `error`, `try/catch/finally`, reset `loading` in `finally`.
- Error message fallback pattern: `err.response?.data?.errorMessage || t('view.error_default')`.
- Success feedback via `showFlash(t('common.saved'))` from `@/lib/flash`.

## Styling
- Tailwind utility classes only, with theme tokens (`text-theme-text`, `bg-theme-bg`, `border-theme-border`) and shared classes (`input-field`, `btn-primary`). No scoped `<style>` blocks.
- Disable inputs and submit buttons while `loading`.
